{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R59"],
      "pins": ["R59.1", "R59.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R59 has a value field of \"24k\" but its description says \"24Ω\" and its MPN is \"FRC0805J240TSD\", a 24Ω part. The SPICE deck also models R59 as 24k.",
      "expected": "The value should match the part metadata and intended role. A 24k resistor across VOUTP/VOUTN is a plausible bleeder; a 24Ω part would be a heavy load, especially on a PoE-derived rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R59\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R59 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled with the specified MPN (24Ω), R59 will present a near-short across VOUTP/VOUTN, causing excessive current and possible damage. If the 24k value is intended, the BOM part is wrong and the board will not match the schematic.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U33", "U50"],
      "pins": ["U33.5", "U50.5"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U33-VP-Pad5)", "unconnected-(U50-VP-Pad5)"],
      "observed": "The VP/VCC pins (pin 5) of U33 and U50 are marked as no-connect/unconnected in the netlist.",
      "expected": "For TPD4E1U06 / AOZ8904CIL ESD protection arrays, the VP pin must be connected to the positive supply rail of the protected interface (e.g., +3V3 or +5V) to clamp positive ESD transients.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"334\") (name \"unconnected-(U33-VP-Pad5)\") (node (ref \"U33\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VP\") (pintype \"unspecified+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"364\") (name \"unconnected-(U50-VP-Pad5)\") (node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VP\") (pintype \"unspecified+no_connect\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet ESD protection is incomplete; positive ESD events may not be properly clamped, increasing the risk of damage to the Ethernet interface.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain two anomalies: R59 has a value of 24k while its description and MPN specify a 24Ω part, and the VP/VCC pins of the Ethernet ESD protection devices U33 and U50 are left unconnected. Both are deviations from sound design practice and would affect board reliability or assembly."
}

